A||N||11||kornholio||where is the air breather located?||||5||
Z||000000||kornholio||12-19-1999||12:53 PM||||I was in the local auto parts store today, and I saw some air breathers.  So I decided to look up the one for my Fiero.  I have never seen anything like that on my engine.  It's kind of retangular in shape with foam on the inside.  Where does this thing go?  I can't find anything that makes reference to an air breather in the Haynes manual.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||01:07 PM||||V6 or 4 cyl?  The stock one for the 4 cyl is round and on top.  It looks like one from all of the old V8 cars with carbs.  Either it's for a 2.8 or it isn't stock.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||12-19-1999||01:15 PM||||Mine's a V6.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||12-19-1999||02:08 PM||||On the V6, you have to remove the driver side louvered vent to get to the air cleaner. I was thinking that on my 85 GT it was round though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||12-19-1999||02:30 PM||||Rectangular? With foam on the inside? Only thing I can think of that matches that description is the PCV breather filter. Goes inside the 4 cyl(only) air filter housing, pokes through a hole in the side, and connects to a 3/4"(?) hose. Don't know of anything on a V-6 that looks like that. 85-88 V-6 air filter is round. About 6" diameter, about 6" tall. Don't think it uses a PCV filter, at all.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-19-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||12-19-1999||04:53 PM||||The thing I'm talking about is not the air filter.  On the package it says air breather and it has something to do with the PCV.  I'm just not sure where it would go.  Could this be the PCV filter?  What does a PCV filter look like?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||12-20-1999||02:26 AM||||Okay, I could be wrong, but... I don't think the V-6 uses a PCV filter. It gets its air  through a pipe that connects between the front valve cover and the intake duct, between the air filter and the throttle body. This air has already been filtered by the regular air filter. Is your part approximately 1.25 x 3.5 inches, with a foam filter in one side, and a 3/4" hose nipple on the other? The side with the hose nipple is slightly curved? If so, it's a 4 cyl PCV filter. Designed to fit inside the regular air filter housing. Your parts catalog may have some bad info. I don't think you need that filter, at all. Hope this helps.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-20-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||01:53 PM||||Nipples?  Is it getting warm in here or is it just me? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||mutfish||12-20-1999||02:47 PM||||"Slightly curved" nipple.....I think that's for a different forum altogether..........||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||12-21-1999||11:58 AM||||Hmmm... Maybe I shoulda gone here: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000239.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000239.html</A> <BR>(Sorry, Al. Couldn't resist.) <P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-21-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||fiero56||12-29-1999||01:28 PM||||While at Autozone today I remembered this thread. I went over to the filters section, looked up the v-6 Fiero and there was an air breather, just as kornholio mentioned. I found a subscript number, and it made mention to the fuel vapor recovery canister. Do those things have a replaceable filter in them? This filter looked like it would fit. It was rectangular, 3-4 inches long, 2" wide.||||reg||1
Z||000011||HF6582||12-29-1999||04:42 PM||||On the bottom of the canister there is a foam element that can be replaced.<P><BR>Scott||||reg||1
